---
source: crates/aozora-cli/tests/snapshot_cli.rs
expression: "run(&[\"check\", \"--help\"])"
---
Run the lexer over a file and report diagnostics

Usage: aozora check [OPTIONS] [FILE]

Arguments:
  [FILE]
          Input path; pass `-` (or omit) to read from stdin
          
          [default: -]

Options:
  -s, --strict
          Exit non-zero on any diagnostic

  -E, --encoding <ENCODING>
          Source encoding

          Possible values:
          - auto: Detect the source encoding: valid UTF-8 is used as-is, otherwise the bytes are
            decoded as Shift_JIS. The right default — Aozora files ship as Shift_JIS, but UTF-8
            mirrors are common, and the caller should not have to know which they have
          - utf8: Force UTF-8; error if the input is not valid UTF-8
          - sjis: Force Shift_JIS decoding
          
          [default: auto]

      --diagnostic-format <DIAGNOSTIC_FORMAT>
          How to render diagnostics: `human` (graphical snippet, the default on a terminal), `json`
          (the `aozora::wire` envelope, the default when stderr is piped — the machine / agent
          path), or `short` (one grep-able line per diagnostic)

          Possible values:
          - auto:  Graphical (`human`) on a terminal, machine (`json`) when piped
          - human: miette graphical report — source snippet + caret + label + help
          - json:  The `aozora::wire` JSON envelope — the cross-binding machine view
          - short: One grep-able line per diagnostic: `path:offset: severity[code]: msg`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
